/-! # Complex contractions and complex-valued coordinate derivatives (ATLAS-V-01)

B3 local layer, registered in `mission/PHYSICS_BOUNDARY.md` §K. Dimension-generic (`Fin n`, total dimension `n`).

* `rcontr T x u v = Σ_{μ,ν} T_{μν}(x) u^μ v^ν` — real bilinear contraction of a real covariant rank-2 field
  (`Metric n` or `TwoForm n`; both are `Fin n → Fin n → Pt n → ℝ`).
* `ccontr T x u v = Σ_{μ,ν} (T_{μν}(x) : ℂ) u^μ v^ν` — its **complex-bilinear** extension to complex vectors. This
  is the contraction used for null frames (no complex conjugation anywhere).
* `hcontr T x u v = Σ (T_{μν}(x) : ℂ) conj(u^μ) v^ν` — the Hermitian (sesquilinear) form. It is **not** used by the
  frame theory; it exists only for the negative control `Atlas.EinsteinMaxwell.NP.Control`.
* `cpdC i f x` — derivative of the real one-variable slice `u ↦ f (x with xᵢ := u)` of a complex-valued function of
  the **real** coordinates (Mathlib `deriv` over `ℝ` with values in `ℂ`); same slice convention as the registered
  `pd` (A1). No holomorphy is assumed or used.
* `cdir Z f x = Σ_μ Z^μ cpdC μ f x` — derivative along a complex coordinate vector `Z`: the complex-linear
  combination of the real coordinate derivatives.

Bridges proved here: `ccontr` of real vectors is the cast of `rcontr`; `ccontr` is complex-bilinear; `cpdC` of a
cast real function is the cast of `pd` (unconditionally); for a slice-differentiable `f`,
`cpdC f = pd (Re f) + i pd (Im f)`; `cdir` with real components on a real function is the cast of the real
directional derivative; the matrix form `(Eᵀ G E)_{AB} = ccontr g (E·A) (E·B)`. -/

open Complex
open scoped ComplexConjugate Matrix ContDiff

namespace ExactVacuumAtlas.EinsteinMaxwell.NP

variable {n : ℕ}

/-! ### Contractions -/

theorem ccontr_ofReal (T : Fin n → Fin n → Pt n → ℝ) (x : Pt n) (u v : Fin n → ℝ) :
    ccontr T x (fun μ => (u μ : ℂ)) (fun μ => (v μ : ℂ)) = (rcontr T x u v : ℂ) := by
  simp [ccontr, rcontr, ofReal_sum, ofReal_mul]

theorem ccontr_lin_right (T : Fin n → Fin n → Pt n → ℝ) (x : Pt n) (α β : ℂ) (u v w : Fin n → ℂ) :
    ccontr T x w (fun μ => α * u μ + β * v μ) = α * ccontr T x w u + β * ccontr T x w v := by
  simp only [ccontr, Finset.mul_sum, ← Finset.sum_add_distrib]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun μ _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun ν _ => by ring))

theorem ccontr_swap (T : Fin n → Fin n → Pt n → ℝ) (x : Pt n) (u v : Fin n → ℂ) :
    ccontr T x v u = ccontr (fun μ ν => T ν μ) x u v := by
  simp only [ccontr]
  rw [Finset.sum_comm]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun μ _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun ν _ => by ring))

theorem ccontr_antisymm {T : Fin n → Fin n → Pt n → ℝ} {x : Pt n} (hT : ∀ i j, T i j x = -T j i x)
    (u v : Fin n → ℂ) : ccontr T x v u = -ccontr T x u v := by
  rw [ccontr_swap]
  simp only [ccontr, ← Finset.sum_neg_distrib]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun μ _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun ν _ => by rw [hT ν μ, ofReal_neg]; ring))

